# dvi_tx_pll: `dvi_tx` with its five-times clock asked of the device's
# PLL through a `clock_mhz` attribute on an undriven net. The board must
# say what `clk_ref` is with a `create_clock`, which is what the PLL is
# fed from. A package of its own rather than a second module in
# `dvi_tx`'s, because a project build loses a top that another module
# of the same sources instantiates with a parameter override: see
# `a_project_top_that_is_also_instantiated_with_an_override_is_lost`.
name dvi_tx_pll
version 1.0.0
license MIT
description "dvi_tx with its five-times pixel clock generated by the device's PLL"

top dvi_tx_pll
target ice40
target ecp5

source rtl/dvi_tx_pll.v

depends dvi_tx ^1.0.0

param MODE int 0 0..2

port clk_ref in
port rst_n in
port pix_en out
port de out
port frame out
port x out 12
port y out 12
port r in 8
port g in 8
port b in 8
port tmds_d0 out 2
port tmds_d1 out 2
port tmds_d2 out 2
port tmds_clk out 2
